nt methods. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> Therefore, the answer is 347410. <|User|>Thank you for walking me through the standard algorithm. It's clear and straightforward. You're welcome! The standard algorithm is a reliable and efficient method for multiplying large numbers. If you have any more questions or need further clarification on any topic, feel free to ask. <|User|>Could you also show me how to solve this using the lattice method? <think>\nCertainly! The lattice method is a visual and systematic way to multiply numbers. It uses a grid to organize the multiplication of each digit. Let's solve the problem using the lattice method.\n...\n<answer>\nTo solve the multiplication of 952 and 365 using the lattice method, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. **Set up the lattice grid**: Draw a 2x2 grid because we are multiplying a 3-digit number by a 3-digit number. Each cell in the grid will have two diagonals.\n\n2. **Write the numbers on the top and left sides of the grid**:\n```\n  952\n\u00d7 365\n-----\n```\n3. **Fill in the grid**:\n   - Write the digits of 952 along the top of the grid and the digits of 365 along the left side of the grid.\n   - Multiply each digit of 952 by each digit of 365 and place the result in the corresponding cell, splitting the result into tens and units.\n\nHere's the grid filled in:\n```\n  9 | 5 | 2\n ---------\n 3 |   |   |\n 6 |   |   |\n 5 |   |   |\n---------\n```\n4. **Multiply each digit**:\n   - 9 \u00d7 3 = 27 (write 2 in the tens diagonal and 7 in the units diagonal)\n   - 9 \u00d7 6 = 54 (write 5 in the tens diagonal and 4 in the units diagonal)\n   - 9 \u00d7 5 = 45 (write 4 in the tens diagonal and 5 in the units diagonal)\n   - 5 \u00d7 3 = 15 (write 1 in the tens diagonal and 5 in the units diagonal)\n   - 5 \u00d7 6 = 30 (write 3 in the tens diagonal and 0 in the units diagonal)\n   - 5 \u00d7 5 = 25 (write 2 in the tens diagonal and 5 in the units diagonal)\n   - 2 \u00d7 3 = 6 (write 6 in the tens diagonal and 0 in the unit