ltiplying each digit step by step. Let's solve \\(141 \\times 636\\) using the column method.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. **Write the numbers one below the other:**\n   ```\n     141\n   \u00d7 636\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply 141 by 6 (the units digit of 636):**\n   ```\n     141\n   \u00d7   6\n   -----\n     846\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply 141 by 30 (the tens digit of 636, shifted one place to the left):**\n   ```\n     141\n   \u00d7  30\n   -----\n    4230\n   ```\n\n4. **Multiply 141 by 600 (the hundreds digit of 636, shifted two places to the left):**\n   ```\n     141\n   \u00d7 600\n   -----\n   84600\n   ```\n\n5. **Add the results of these multiplications:**\n   ```\n     846\n   +4230\n   +84600\n   -----\n   88676\n   ```\n\nSo, the product of 141 and 636 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{88676}\n\\]\n\nThis confirms that the product is indeed 88,676. <|User|>Thank you for your help with all these methods. Can you also show me how to solve this using the grid method, but this time with a different number, say 123 and 456?\n<|Assistant|>\nCertainly! Let's solve \\(123 \\times 456\\) using the grid method. The grid method breaks down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts by using a grid.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. **Set up the grid:**\n   - Draw a 2x3 grid (since 123 has 3 digits and 456 has 3 digits).\n   ```\n     123\n   \u00d7 456\n   ------\n   ```\n\n2. **Write the digits in the grid:**\n   - Place the digits of 123 along the top of the grid.\n   - Place the digits of 456 along the left side of the grid.\n   ```\n     1 | 2 | 3\n   \u00d7 4 | 5 | 6\n   ------\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply each digit:**\n   - Multiply each digit in the top row by each digit in the left column and write the result in the corresponding cell of the grid.\n   ```\n     1 | 2 | 3\n   \u00d7 4 | 5 | 6\n   ------\n    4 | 10 | 18\n   2 | 10 | 12\n   3 | 15 | 18\n   ```\n\n4. **Add the areas of the smaller rectangles:**\n   - Add the numbers in each diagonal, starting from the bottom right.\n   - If the sum is a two-digit number, carry over the tens digit to the next diagonal.\n   ```\n     4 | 10 | 18\n   +10 | 10 | 12\n   +15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n    4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------\n   4 | 10 | 18\n   10 | 10 | 12\n   15 | 15 | 18\n   ------