 all these partial products:\n\\[ 210000 + 12000 + 1500 + 14000 + 800 + 100 + 3500 + 200 + 25 = 252125 \\]\n\nSo, the product of 325 and 745 is \\( 252125 \\).\n\nIn the partial products method, we break down each number into its place values and then multiply each part separately. By summing all these partial products, we get the final product.\n</think>\n<answer>\nUsing the partial products method, we break down the numbers 325 and 745 into their place values and then multiply each part separately. Here's the step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. Break down 325 into 300, 20, and 5:\n   \\[ 325 = 300 + 20 + 5 \\]\n\n2. Break down 745 into 700, 40, and 5:\n   \\[ 745 = 700 + 40 + 5 \\]\n\n3. Multiply each part of 325 by each part of 745:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   300 \\times 700 &= 210000 \\\\\n   300 \\times 40 &= 12000 \\\\\n   300 \\times 5 &= 1500 \\\\\n   20 \\times 700 &= 14000 \\\\\n   20 \\times 40 &= 800 \\\\\n   20 \\times 5 &= 100 \\\\\n   5 \\times 700 &= 3500 \\\\\n   5 \\times 40 &= 200 \\\\\n   5 \\times 5 &= 25 \\\\\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum all the partial products:\n   \\[\n   210000 + 12000 + 1500 + 14000 + 800 + 100 + 3500 + 200 + 25 = 252125\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of 325 and 745 is \\( 252125 \\).\n\nIn the partial products method, we break down each number into its place values and then multiply each part separately, summing the results to get the final product.\n</answer>\nThe answer you provided is correct. Using the partial products method, we break down the numbers 325 and 745 into their place values (300, 20, 5 and 700, 40, 5 respectively) and then multiply each part separately. By summing all these partial products, we find that the product of 325 and 745 is \\( 252125 \\). This method helps in understanding how each step contributes to the final product. <|User|>This is very helpful. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the standard algorithm for multiplication? I find it useful to see all the steps in one pla